<title>USA: Equifax Inc Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Equifax Inc Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>3rd Quarter     Nine Months</p>
<p>				  1996	1995	1996	1995</p>
<p> Operating revenue    $454,986 $412,027 $1,323,612 $1,203,626</p>
<p>Operating income before</p>
<p>     impairment loss     81,041   66,100    221,921   182,853</p>
<p>  Asset impairment loss(A)   --	 --   (10,313)	  --</p>
<p>   Operating income	81,041   66,100    211,608   182,853</p>
<p>   Other income, net	  757    2,233	9,986     6,479</p>
<p>   Interest expense     (5,800)  (5,398)   (16,220)  (15,319)</p>
<p> Income before taxes     75,998   62,935    205,374   174,013</p>
<p> Net income		  45,804   37,981    123,779   103,267</p>
<p> Net EPS			  .32	.25	  .85	 .68</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs	    144,752  151,618    145,781   152,305</p>
<p>		    (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>(A) In accordance with the FASB 121, &quot;Accounting for the Impairment of Long-Lived Assets and FOR Long-Lived Assets to be Disposed Of,&quot; in June 1996, company recorded a loss to write off certain intangible assets in the Healthcare division of its General Information Services segment.</p>
